 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:10:15.002007Z",
 "text": "Under section 106 of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a landlord may require a tenant to pay a rent deposit on or before entering into the tenancy agreement (s. 106(1)). Where rent is paid monthly, the deposit may be up to one month's rent (s. 106(2)), and the landlord must apply it strictly toward the rent for the last rent period before the tenancy terminates (s. 106(10)). Because this clause complies with all of those statutory conditions, it is valid and enforceable.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 106",
